# Parallel PRs lower different lines of the size baselines; union merge avoids
# conflicts, and the gate re-validates after merge (a stale higher value only
# shows as SLACK).
#
# When two branches change the SAME row, union keeps both copies. The gate
# handles that itself: scripts/check-skill-size.sh reads a repeated key as the
# min of its values plus every copy's comments, fails check mode with
# "DUPLICATE: <key>", and `make skill-baseline` collapses it to one row.
#
# No custom merge driver on purpose: a driver needs `git config` in every
# clone, and GitHub's server-side PR merges never run one, so it would not
# cover the merges that actually produce duplicates. The gate-side check does.
scripts/skill-size-baseline.tsv merge=union
scripts/skill-context-baseline.tsv merge=union
